IMPORT prelude

-- Fire Safety Act 1993 (Singapore) -- the offences an ordinary person, building owner or contractor meets: false alarms and fire
-- hydrants (ss 24, 25), specified fire hazards (s 2, ss 26, 27), fire hazard abatement notices (s 28(5)), fire certificates (s 35),
-- at-risk premises and who counts as owner or occupier in Part 3 (ss 38(5), 40), alarm monitoring (s 53), fire safety works,
-- supervision, fire safety certificates and change of use (ss 56, 58, 60, 61), and the penalty machinery (ss 101, 107 and the
-- maximum penalties stated in the sections encoded).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FSA1993.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 18/12/2023"; the latest amending Act annotated in the body is
-- 40/2019. Section numbers follow the BODY; the arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with it.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to offences with decision content. Not
-- encoded: registered inspectors and fire safety engineers (registration, discipline, inquiry panels), powers of entry and in the
-- event of fire, the Commissioner's emergency abatement and closure powers (ss 29-34), Emergency Response Plans (s 37), alarm
-- monitoring licensing beyond s 53, regulated fire safety products (Part 5), the petroleum and flammable materials licensing
-- scheme (Part 6) except the pipeline-damage penalty, appeals, and anything left to regulations (including which offences are
-- compoundable and which buildings are designated under s 35).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fire Safety Act 1993 -- offences`

§§ `2 -- specified fire hazard`

-- s 2: "specified fire hazard", in relation to a building, means (a) "the overcrowding of a building that is a public building such as
-- might render escape in the event of fire more difficult"; (b) "any fire safety measure in the building that is not in proper working
-- order, whether because of lack of proper maintenance or for any other reason"; or (c) "the obstruction of escape routes,
-- passageways, common property or limited common property of the building such as might render escape in the event of fire more
-- difficult".
DECLARE `Building condition` HAS
    `the building is a public building` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is overcrowded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fire safety measure is not in proper working order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an escape route, passageway or common property is obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `escape in a fire might be made more difficult` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Building condition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a specified fire hazard` IF
        (`the condition`'s `it is overcrowded` AND `the condition`'s `the building is a public building`
            AND `the condition`'s `escape in a fire might be made more difficult`)
    OR  `the condition`'s `a fire safety measure is not in proper working order`
    OR  (`the condition`'s `an escape route, passageway or common property is obstructed`
            AND `the condition`'s `escape in a fire might be made more difficult`)

§§ `24, 25 -- fire hydrants and false alarms`

-- s 24(1): an offence for any person who "(a) not being a member of the Force takes water from a fire hydrant other than for the
-- extinguishment of a fire without the consent of the Commissioner or the Public Utilities Board"; or "(b) wilfully damages a fire
-- hydrant" -- fine up to $5,000 (no imprisonment is stated). (2): a person convicted under (1)(b) is ALSO liable to pay compensation to
-- the Public Utilities Board for repair or replacement.
GIVEN `is a member of the Force` IS A BOOLEAN, `took water from a hydrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was to put out a fire` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had consent of the Commissioner or the PUB` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully damaged a hydrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits a hydrant offence` IF
        (`took water from a hydrant` AND (NOT `is a member of the Force`) AND (NOT `it was to put out a fire`)
            AND (NOT `had consent of the Commissioner or the PUB`))
    OR  `wilfully damaged a hydrant`

GIVEN `wilfully damaged a hydrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is also liable to compensate the PUB` IF `wilfully damaged a hydrant`

-- s 25(1): "Any person who knowingly gives or causes to be given a false alarm of fire to the Force or to the police" -- $5,000 or
-- 3 months or both. (2): "false alarm of fire" includes "a false call for the ambulance or other services provided by the Force".
DECLARE `Call` IS ONE OF
    `a fire`
    `an ambulance`
    `another Force service`

GIVEN `the call was for` IS A `Call`, `the alarm was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `the caller knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made to the Force or the police` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the false alarm offence` IF
    `the alarm was false` AND `the caller knew it was false` AND `made to the Force or the police`

§§ `26, 27 -- causing or tolerating a specified fire hazard`

-- s 26(1): an owner or occupier of a building commits an offence "if the owner or occupier causes, or does or omits to do anything that
-- is likely to cause, a specified fire hazard to arise at the building". (3) intent need not be proved; (4) "a strict liability
-- offence". (2): an owner or occupier commits an offence if he "knows or ought to know" there is, or is likely to be, a specified fire
-- hazard "but does not take reasonable steps to abate" or prevent it.
-- No penalty is stated in s 26, so s 107 (general penalty) applies.
GIVEN `is an owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused or was likely to cause a specified fire hazard` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intended it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 26(1) offence` IF
    `is an owner or occupier` AND `caused or was likely to cause a specified fire hazard`

GIVEN `is an owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to know of an actual or likely specified fire hazard` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps to abate or prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 26(2) offence` IF
    `is an owner or occupier` AND `knew or ought to know of an actual or likely specified fire hazard`
        AND (NOT `took reasonable steps to abate or prevent it`)

-- s 27: ANY person commits an offence by an act or omission that causes or is likely to cause "(a) any fire safety measure in the
-- premises not to be in proper working order; or (b) any escape route, passageway, common property ... to be obstructed -- (i) such as
-- might render escape in the event of fire more difficult; and (ii) which obstruction cannot be easily removed by an individual
-- escaping from a fire", where the person "knows or ought to know" of that effect. Not strict liability, unlike s 26(1).
DECLARE `Act or omission` HAS
    `it disables a fire safety measure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it obstructs an escape route` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the obstruction might make escape more difficult` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the obstruction can easily be removed by someone escaping` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew or ought to have known the effect` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Act or omission`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 27 offence` IF
        (`the act`'s `it disables a fire safety measure`
            OR (`the act`'s `it obstructs an escape route` AND `the act`'s `the obstruction might make escape more difficult`
                    AND (NOT `the act`'s `the obstruction can easily be removed by someone escaping`)))
    AND `the act`'s `the person knew or ought to have known the effect`

§§ `28(5) -- fire hazard abatement notice`

-- s 28(5): where a fire hazard abatement notice has been served and the person "(a) fails to comply with any of the requirements within
-- the time specified in the notice; or (b) fails to take such steps as are specified in the notice to prevent the recurrence", the
-- person is guilty of an offence "whether or not an order under section 31 has been made". No penalty stated: s 107 applies.
GIVEN `a notice was served on the person` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied within the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took the specified steps against recurrence` IS A BOOLEAN, `a court order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the abatement notice offence` IF
    `a notice was served on the person` AND ((NOT `complied within the time`) OR (NOT `took the specified steps against recurrence`))

§ `Part 3 -- fire prevention in buildings`

§§ `35 -- fire certificate`

-- s 35(1): applies only to buildings the Minister designates by Gazette notification. (2): a person must not "(a) occupy or use a
-- building; or (b) permit a building owned or managed by the person to be occupied or used, unless there is a fire certificate
-- authorising the occupation or use". (5): the prosecution need not prove the defendant "knew that there was no fire certificate"; (6)
-- strict liability. No penalty stated: s 107 applies.
GIVEN `the building is designated` IS A BOOLEAN, `occupies, uses or permits use` IS A BOOLEAN, `a fire certificate authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew there was no fire certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the fire certificate offence` IF
    `the building is designated` AND `occupies, uses or permits use` AND (NOT `a fire certificate authorises it`)

§§ `38(5), 40 -- at-risk premises; owner or occupier`

-- s 38(5): premises are at-risk premises where "(a) the risk of fire occurring in or spreading in or from the particular premises is
-- higher than that for other premises in general; or (b) the age, physical ability or such other characteristics of the individuals who
-- occupy or frequent the particular premises render escape by these individuals in the event of fire more difficult". At-risk premises
-- can be required (s 38(4)) to keep a larger Company Emergency Response Team, extra equipment, and to give 14 days' notice of a change in
-- ownership or occupancy.
GIVEN `the fire risk is higher than for premises in general` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupants' age, ability or characteristics make escape harder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are at-risk premises` IF
    `the fire risk is higher than for premises in general` OR `the occupants' age, ability or characteristics make escape harder`

-- s 40: "In this Part" (Part 3 only), for a building on land in an approved strata subdivision plan, references to the owner or occupier
-- "do not include references to the subsidiary proprietors or tenants of any part of the building". Part 2 (ss 26-34) has no such
-- exclusion.
DECLARE `Part` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2`
    `Part 3`

GIVEN `the Part` IS A `Part`, `owns or occupies part of the building` IS A BOOLEAN, `the building is strata subdivided` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is only a subsidiary proprietor or tenant of a unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as an owner or occupier` IF
    `owns or occupies part of the building`
        AND (NOT (`the Part` EQUALS `Part 3` AND `the building is strata subdivided` AND `is only a subsidiary proprietor or tenant of a unit`))

§ `Parts 3B and 4 -- alarm monitoring and fire safety works`

§§ `53 -- cancelling a request without checking`

-- s 53(1): where a request is made to the Commissioner to extinguish a fire (or deal with an escape of petroleum or flammable
-- material) at a building, the licensee providing alarm monitoring services "must take all reasonable steps to ascertain that there is
-- no fire ... before cancelling the request". (2) $10,000 or 6 months or both. (3) a "request" includes an alarm signal transmitted to
-- the Force's alarm monitoring network.
GIVEN `the licensee cancelled the request` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps to ascertain there was no fire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 53 offence` IF
    `the licensee cancelled the request` AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps to ascertain there was no fire`)

§§ `56, 58 -- approved plans and supervision`

-- s 56(1): a person must not carry out, "or permit or authorise the carrying out of", fire safety works "(a) before the Commissioner has
-- approved all the plans ... or (b) otherwise than in accordance with the plans approved". (2) $200,000 or 2 years or both, and $1,000 a
-- day for a continuing offence.
GIVEN `carried out or authorised fire safety works` IS A BOOLEAN, `all plans were approved first` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the works followed the approved plans` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the unapproved works offence` IF
    `carried out or authorised fire safety works` AND ((NOT `all plans were approved first`) OR (NOT `the works followed the approved plans`))

-- s 58(1): a person must not commence or carry out fire safety works "except under the supervision of an appropriate qualified person or
-- fire safety engineer appointed under section 57". (2) $200,000 or 2 years or both, and $2,000 a day for a continuing offence -- twice
-- the daily rate for unapproved works.
GIVEN `carried out fire safety works` IS A BOOLEAN, `supervised by an appointed qualified person or fire safety engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the unsupervised works offence` IF
    `carried out fire safety works` AND (NOT `supervised by an appointed qualified person or fire safety engineer`)

§§ `60 -- revoking a fire safety certificate`

-- s 60(8): the Commissioner may revoke a fire safety certificate or temporary fire permit if satisfied that information in the
-- application is "false in a material particular", or that the registered inspector's certificate is false. (9): but "must not revoke
-- ... unless (a) the Commissioner has given a written notice ... to comply ... with such requirements as the Commissioner may specify ...
-- and (b) the person has failed or refused to comply". (12): the decision takes effect on a date "not less than 14 days" from written
-- notification.
GIVEN `the application information or inspector's certificate was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `a written notice to comply was given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person failed or refused to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may revoke the fire safety certificate` IF
    `the application information or inspector's certificate was false` AND `a written notice to comply was given`
        AND `the person failed or refused to comply`

GIVEN `notified on day` IS A NUMBER, `takes effect on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation date is lawful` IF `takes effect on day` MINUS `notified on day` AT LEAST 14

§§ `61 -- change of use`

-- s 61(1): a person who changes the use of premises must, "if such change of use would cause the existing fire safety measures to become
-- inadequate, prior to carrying out the change, apply to the Commissioner for approval". (5) $200,000 or 2 years or both, $1,000 a day.
GIVEN `the change would make existing fire safety measures inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `approval is needed for the change of use` IF `the change would make existing fire safety measures inadequate`

GIVEN `changed the use of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the change would make existing fire safety measures inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applied for approval before the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the change of use offence` IF
    `changed the use of the premises` AND `approval is needed for the change of use` `the change would make existing fire safety measures inadequate`
        AND (NOT `applied for approval before the change`)

§ `Penalties`

§§ `stated penalties, 107 -- general penalty`

-- s 107: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- a fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both, and up
-- to $1,000 a day for a continuing offence. Stated penalties: s 22(2) plate $1,000; s 24 hydrant $5,000; s 25 false alarm $5,000 or 3
-- months; s 36(3) order to install fire safety measures $50,000 or 12 months, $1,000 a day; s 53(2) $10,000 or 6 months; s 56(2)
-- $200,000 or 2 years, $1,000 a day; s 58(2) $200,000 or 2 years, $2,000 a day; s 60(6) registered inspector's false certificate
-- $100,000 or 2 years; s 60(13) fire safety certificate $10,000, $1,000 a day; s 61(5) $200,000 or 2 years, $1,000 a day; s 85(3)
-- damage to a licensed pipeline $100,000 or 12 months, $1,000 a day; s 94 obstruction $10,000 or 6 months; s 109 false information in a
-- licence application $10,000 or 6 months. ss 26, 27, 28(5), 35(4), 37(6), 38(6) and 85(1) state no penalty.
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `removing a hydrant plate`
    `a hydrant offence`
    `a false alarm`
    `causing a specified fire hazard as owner or occupier`
    `causing a fire hazard as any person`
    `failing to comply with an abatement notice`
    `occupying without a fire certificate`
    `failing to install ordered fire safety measures`
    `cancelling an alarm request without checking`
    `fire safety works without approved plans`
    `fire safety works without supervision`
    `a registered inspector's false certificate`
    `breaching fire safety certificate requirements`
    `change of use without approval`
    `unlicensed storage of petroleum`
    `damaging a licensed pipeline`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `false information in a licence application`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `removing a hydrant plate` THEN 1000
    WHEN `a hydrant offence` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a false alarm` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to install ordered fire safety measures` THEN 50000
    WHEN `cancelling an alarm request without checking` THEN 10000
    WHEN `fire safety works without approved plans` THEN 200000
    WHEN `fire safety works without supervision` THEN 200000
    WHEN `a registered inspector's false certificate` THEN 100000
    WHEN `breaching fire safety certificate requirements` THEN 10000
    WHEN `change of use without approval` THEN 200000
    WHEN `damaging a licensed pipeline` THEN 100000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `false information in a licence application` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 10000

-- In months; 0 where the section states a fine only.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `removing a hydrant plate` THEN 0
    WHEN `a hydrant offence` THEN 0
    WHEN `a false alarm` THEN 3
    WHEN `failing to install ordered fire safety measures` THEN 12
    WHEN `cancelling an alarm request without checking` THEN 6
    WHEN `fire safety works without approved plans` THEN 24
    WHEN `fire safety works without supervision` THEN 24
    WHEN `a registered inspector's false certificate` THEN 24
    WHEN `breaching fire safety certificate requirements` THEN 0
    WHEN `change of use without approval` THEN 24
    WHEN `damaging a licensed pipeline` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 6
    WHEN `false information in a licence application` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 6

-- Further fine per day for a continuing offence after conviction; 0 where none is stated.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `removing a hydrant plate` THEN 0
    WHEN `a hydrant offence` THEN 0
    WHEN `a false alarm` THEN 0
    WHEN `cancelling an alarm request without checking` THEN 0
    WHEN `fire safety works without supervision` THEN 2000
    WHEN `a registered inspector's false certificate` THEN 0
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 0
    WHEN `false information in a licence application` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 1000

§§ `101 -- composition`

-- s 101(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower
-- of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000". (2) no further
-- proceedings after payment. Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Offence`, `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
    ELSE 0
